Astral Plane...
Was granted an Angel, promptly pissed him off by putting on =oConflict (and
=oFA). A cockatrice showed up and kindly left a corpse, which I decided to
use. I'm sure #twoweapon with the two silver sabers would have been
sufficient but I figured I'd play the odds with instadeath. I headed right
up the gut bewteen the tackles and fell to Death
which used up my only "oLS. HP had been about 230, resurrected it was only
140. Death was still going after me when I ducked around a soldier ant,
putting him between Death and myself. I could almost feel his angry hands
reaching around the ant in frustration. Not to be. Hopefully my choice
would pay off and I wouldn't have to face him coming back.
I stoned a few more Angels and Priests, moved into the temple and took of
the =oConflict. Check out the Priest.....hold breath...Lugh. Cha-ching!
Offer the amluet and I'm on my way.

Loosing all my stuff made me take a new approach to the planes and the game
was a lot more fun for it. Of course, I'm also lucky to be alive an would
have rather gone through with my SDSM and other stuff. On the other hand,
this way I feel a certain kinship to Lancelot and his approach to
dragon-slaying (according to the Steinbeck version anyway...)

